# Local S3 integration-test config. Copy to `.env.test` (gitignored) and edit.
#
# Non-secret only — no credentials here. `npm run test:integration` relocates
# s3cab's home (S3CAB_HOME) but leaves HOME alone, so the AWS SDK reads your
# ~/.aws profile/SSO session directly. AWS_PROFILE just picks which profile.
#
# Precedence note: these are loaded with Node's --env-file, which does NOT
# override a variable already set in your shell — so an exported AWS_PROFILE
# wins over the one here. s3cab's startup line reports which it used and from
# where, e.g. "Using AWS profile: X (from your environment)".

S3CAB_TEST_BUCKET=your-test-bucket
AWS_REGION=us-east-1
# AWS_PROFILE=your-profile   # uncomment to use a non-default ~/.aws profile

# Uncomment for verbose output (full error causes) while debugging a failing test:
# S3CAB_DEBUG=1

# Point the suite at a non-AWS S3-compatible provider (Cloudflare R2, Backblaze
# B2, MinIO, …); credentials still come from the AWS_* vars / your ~/.aws profile:
# AWS_ENDPOINT_URL_S3=https://your-endpoint
